            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "By unique prime factorisation, each denominator is $2^m3^n$ for exactly one pair of non-negative integers $m,n$. Expanding the following product therefore gives every required term exactly once, including $1$ when $m=n=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\left(1+\\frac12+\\frac1{2^2}+\\cdots\\right)\\left(1+\\frac13+\\frac1{3^2}+\\cdots\\right)\\\\S&=\\frac1{1-\\frac12}\\times\\frac1{1-\\frac13}\\\\S&=2\\times\\frac32\\\\S&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
